{"seq":33,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.547Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-1 Embedded SQLite through Node's built-in driver: Store data in SQLite using node:sqlite, with all SQL confined to repository and analytics classes.","rationale":"The requirement is a single command and no external services. The built-in driver needs no native build step, so installation cannot fail on a compiler or a blocked binary download. Confining SQL to two classes keeps a later move to a networked database local to them.","alternatives":["PostgreSQL: the right choice for several instances, but it is an external service","better-sqlite3: mature, but a native module that must be compiled or downloaded at install time","In-memory map: no durability"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"a7a867f232ef5181fae6390d3e23d91f2c0165b38461e5293319d544efdff9a7","hash":"7d6721daadb16fff0c0cf7219eacbf4f0b790b44cbed790edc80f74fd10509ea"}
{"seq":34,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.547Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-2 Random codes, uniqueness enforced by the primary key: Generate 7 random base62 characters from a cryptographic source, insert, and retry with a new code if the insert reports a clash, up to 5 times.","rationale":"Random codes cannot be enumerated or guessed in sequence. Letting the primary key decide uniqueness removes the read-then-write race of checking first.","alternatives":["Sequential counter encoded in base62: short, but every link is discoverable by counting","Hash of the URL: two callers shortening the same URL would share a code and its statistics"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"7d6721daadb16fff0c0cf7219eacbf4f0b790b44cbed790edc80f74fd10509ea","hash":"69d8312b1e49c4f50fae73e418dcc772c591743ef18703786d4c633db5b02197"}
{"seq":35,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.547Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-3 302 with no-store for redirects: Redirect with 302 and Cache-Control: no-store.","rationale":"Click analytics is a requirement. A cached 301 means repeat visits never reach the service, and a link could never be changed or withdrawn later.","alternatives":["301: one request fewer for repeat visitors, at the cost of analytics and control"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"69d8312b1e49c4f50fae73e418dcc772c591743ef18703786d4c633db5b02197","hash":"6123d93fc6284280082a2052af40d47dd944dcc2afdcf7f5589aa455ba289e90"}
{"seq":36,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.547Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-4 Click recording is asynchronous and best-effort: A redirect pushes a click onto a bounded in-memory queue. A timer writes the queue in one transaction together with the per-link totals. When the queue is full, clicks are dropped and counted.","rationale":"The requirement states that recording a click must never slow down or fail a redirect. A bounded queue keeps memory fixed under load, and one transaction per batch keeps the event rows and the totals consistent.","alternatives":["Write synchronously in the redirect: exact counts, but a slow or locked database would slow or fail redirects","External message queue: durable, but an external service"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"6123d93fc6284280082a2052af40d47dd944dcc2afdcf7f5589aa455ba289e90","hash":"c7ba897ab2052b9948e3e70c7ab961acfaba6c35d7d605bb2cc54d6339d15fda"}
{"seq":37,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.547Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-5 Per-client token bucket on the management API only: Rate limit /api/* per client address with an in-process token bucket whose key count is bounded. Redirects are not limited.","rationale":"Link creation is the write an attacker can abuse; redirects are the product and are a single indexed read. The key bound stops a flood of distinct addresses from exhausting memory.","alternatives":["Shared limiter in Redis: needed for several instances, but an external service","Limit redirects too: would throttle legitimate traffic to a popular link"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"c7ba897ab2052b9948e3e70c7ab961acfaba6c35d7d605bb2cc54d6339d15fda","hash":"bc5c1df8dd868b5d822120bd9de36d5f67afcf4dfa2190911d4cf3ffd68fd5d1"}
{"seq":38,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.547Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-6 Store the referrer's host only, and no client address: Reduce the Referer header to its host before it is queued. Do not store or log the client address.","rationale":"A full referrer URL can carry personal data in its path or query. Host-level data answers the stated question (top referrers) without holding personal data.","alternatives":["Store the full referrer URL: more detail than was asked for, with a privacy cost"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"bc5c1df8dd868b5d822120bd9de36d5f67afcf4dfa2190911d4cf3ffd68fd5d1","hash":"671fc720b8b55c86e70cf9a29a30dc51c445cc94b2bfb56d1659ffaecfa7604e"}
{"seq":39,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.548Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-7 Errors as RFC 9457 problem documents: Every error response is application/problem+json with a stable machine-readable code. Unexpected errors are logged in full and returned as a generic 500.","rationale":"Clients get one error shape to handle, and internal detail never leaves the process.","alternatives":["Ad-hoc JSON error bodies per route"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"671fc720b8b55c86e70cf9a29a30dc51c445cc94b2bfb56d1659ffaecfa7604e","hash":"88b10974e657cf67dd8b813bbdea31a09797686dba0708e68aa69f7c978e8151"}
{"seq":40,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.548Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"DECISION_RECORDED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"decision":"ADR-8 Run the TypeScript sources directly: Use Node's built-in type stripping; type-check with tsc --noEmit as a separate step.","rationale":"No build output to keep in sync and a single start command. The cost is a minimum Node version of 22.18 and a restriction to erasable TypeScript syntax, which the compiler enforces.","alternatives":["Compile to dist/ with tsc: works on older Node versions, adds a build step","tsx or ts-node: an extra runtime dependency"],"basedOn":"d1a62b5666fdfabcd61b08964cfe1320107d137ca494f27278b63a2dda372e54"},"prevHash":"88b10974e657cf67dd8b813bbdea31a09797686dba0708e68aa69f7c978e8151","hash":"c550605d1059ffb8ff34ccb6ae0376157256fff1b9ff76e1f1cca2269beae7a6"}
{"seq":41,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.548Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"ARTIFACT_PUBLISHED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"agent:architecture"},"data":{"name":"design","version":1,"hash":"fa7e1e9ce7c0d5831e20c40c8acba701743df4ea08e6f764e7a4772c784ed763","status":"proposed","derivedFrom":{"requirement-spec":"d0cb49a456d820d3835e599c54a06acbda2f2b6c036f1a504840ba40af51c71b","plan":"8b2271eddda34d7b67802e1e182344a49646be3c736336a577cb6e6a5232f5aa"}},"prevHash":"c550605d1059ffb8ff34ccb6ae0376157256fff1b9ff76e1f1cca2269beae7a6","hash":"5ce8cc90a215347196e383ae91a29a34d03bc5113bdc6843f4b5706000811f13"}
{"seq":42,"ts":"2026-10-02T00:56:50.548Z","runId":"failure-fallback","type":"APPROVAL_REQUESTED","stageId":"architecture","actor":{"kind":"engine","id":"orchestrator"},"data":{"phase":"after","kind":"approval","subjectHash":"6f364b631206b1f66a465821f0bd7e604d7b07bf77e1bca3808e7edca77709fb","reasons":["The design changes the database schema.","The design changes the public API (additive).","The design adds or changes dependencies: fastify, zod, typescript, vitest, @types/node."]},"prevHash":"5ce8cc90a215347196e383ae91a29a34d03bc5113bdc6843f4b5706000811f13","hash":"83af5900fa57f58ab143d3dcd87365f3d874d0a9a2028131b65824681beee977"}
